method for devising words for all languages. I would disagree with that &
argue that it's better to use autonyms where you can (the majority? the vas=
t
majority?), and exonyms otherwise. But I'm not here to stand in the way of
progress.

Is there, actually, an argument for including the ISO code for the language
family? Because I still can't wrap my brain around that. And I'd like to.
(And that is my main point, which I failed to make clear earlier.)

